@startuml
title mp-dance-lora — Low-latency Dance VJ (16 GB RAM)
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

actor "Performer" as Human
component "Camera / Capture" as Camera
component "Python\nMediaPipe Pose\nLive landmarks + timestamps" as Pose
queue "Latest-pose slot\nBounded / overwrite stale frame" as PoseBus
component "Rust Motion Engine\nMotion buffer · loop · blend\nContinue when performer is still" as Motion
component "Rust Renderer\nGPU / wgpu · trails · silhouettes" as Render
component "Projector\nFullscreen output" as Projector
component "JavaScript UI\nControls · calibration · status" as UI
database "dance.poses.sqlite" as DB
file "poses.jsonl" as JSONL
component "Kaggle / Python\nOffline evaluation and training" as Kaggle

Human --> Camera
Camera --> Pose : frames (latest-frame policy)
Pose --> PoseBus : landmarks
PoseBus --> Motion : newest pose only
Motion --> Render : render state / motion
Render --> Projector : low-latency frames
UI <--> Motion : OSC / WebSocket / local IPC\n(select one transport)
Pose --> DB : async recording
DB --> JSONL : export
JSONL --> Kaggle : upload when needed
Kaggle --> JSONL : metrics / prepared sequences

note bottom of PoseBus
Do not build an unbounded frame queue.
Drop stale frames to prevent latency growth.
end note

note bottom of Motion
Live movement drives the output when available.
When movement stops, continue from buffered motion.
Keep offline model training out of the live loop.
end note
@enduml
